+Core shutdown previously closed the SDK while application-owned profile watchers were still awaiting subscription. Actual onboarding completed its signed write, then failed with StreamClosedException during teardown. The corrected order cancels and joins application producers before SDK shutdown. A single retained owned cleanup Deferred is shared by stop and closeAndJoin; stop initiates cleanup and cannot synchronously await its result. External owners use closeAndJoin. Calls from Core-owned descendants reject before cancellation or NonCancellable replacement. Every lifecycle cleanup is attempted; repeated close retains the same failure; telemetry drains before transports close; ConcreteCore closes its owned raw HTTP RPC client, while injected clients are borrowed. The fixture preserves an original test failure and suppresses cleanup failure onto it.
