+
+## Existing application confidentiality debt
+
+Locker read/subscribe routes provide no account read ACL or confidentiality by design. Its locks authenticate mutations. In this preserved Social snapshot, createProfile stores ProfileSource.privateKey in an ordinary plaintext locker under the account room. A separate actual HTTP fixture probe created a real profile, then used a fresh RoomServiceRpc without any session credentials to GetLocker. Reconstructing a P256 key from the returned plaintext produced the profile's public key. The deliberately negative assertion failed with a generic boolean-only message; no private key or plaintext bytes were logged.
+
+This proves an application confidentiality gap in the fixture's public read boundary. Production App Check is independently configurable and defaults off; attestation alone does not establish account authorization for a private room. This probe does not claim to bypass an enabled production attestation verifier or other deployment controls. Account secrets require application encryption or an account-authorized read boundary. Neither Social encryption nor Locker read policy was changed by this consumer verification. The probe is retained as evidence outside the normal test source set, not reported as a passing gate or a new Locker finding.
